import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const inventoryCommand =
  "npx --yes @modelcontextprotocol/conformance@0.2.0-alpha.11 list --requirements 2026-07-28";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="MCP conformance claims stop at the evidence."
  description="Inspect the frozen official runner inventory, the strict Tool profile evidence, and what StateKnot deliberately does not claim."
  section="MCP conformance status"
>
  <aside
    class="docs-callout docs-callout--boundary"
    aria-labelledby="mcp-conformance-boundary-title"
  >
    <h2 id="mcp-conformance-boundary-title">Current claim</h2>
    <p>
      StateKnot implements a strict durable MCP 2026-07-28 Remote Tool profile.
      It does not claim complete official MCP client, server, or SDK-tier
      conformance.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <section aria-labelledby="mcp-conformance-input-title">
    <h2 id="mcp-conformance-input-title">Frozen evaluation input</h2>
    <p>The inventory was refreshed on 2026-09-02 with:</p>
    <div class="docs-code" data-code-block>
      <div class="docs-code-head">
        <span>Shell · official requirement inventory</span>
        <button
          class="copy-button affordance"
          type="button"
          data-copy-button
          data-copy-target="mcp-conformance-inventory-code"
        >
          <span data-copy-label aria-live="polite">Copy</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <pre
        id="mcp-conformance-inventory-code"
        tabindex="0"><code>{inventoryCommand}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <dl class="docs-definition-list">
      <div>
        <dt>Runner</dt>
        <dd><code>@modelcontextprotocol/conformance@0.2.0-alpha.11</code></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Source identity</dt>
        <dd><code>c321dd32035556e6769d3724a8ee97d87c3faaac</code></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Requirement revision</dt>
        <dd><code>2026-07-28</code></dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Inventory</dt>
        <dd>69 scored scenarios: 37 server and 32 client scenarios.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <p>
      See the <a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/conformance"
        >official conformance repository</a
      > and the <a
        href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/blob/main/docs/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools.mdx"
        >MCP 2026-07-28 Tool specification</a
      > for the authoritative runner and protocol requirements.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="mcp-conformance-difference-title">
    <h2 id="mcp-conformance-difference-title">
      The strict profile is not the general client role
    </h2>
    <p>
      <code>McpRemoteTool</code> requires reviewed local input and output schemas,
      byte-identical remote schemas, a pinned server implementation, and complete
      <code>structuredContent</code> validated locally. The official required
      <code>tools_call</code> client fixture advertises no output schema and returns
      text without structured content. A general client can call that fixture; the
      strict StateKnot binding must reject it.
    </p>
    <p>
      StateKnot will not loosen its production contract only for the runner and
      will not turn an expected failure into a conformance badge. A separate
      general MCP client surface is required before broader interoperability can
      be claimed honestly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="mcp-conformance-evidence-title">
    <h2 id="mcp-conformance-evidence-title">Executable evidence that exists</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The strict loopback contract proves protocol headers, discovery order,
        exact server/schema pins, attempt authorization, bounded calls, drift
        rejection, and reconcile-first lost writes.
      </li>
      <li>
        The PostgreSQL 16/17 durable contract proves the invocation is
        <code>Executing</code> before MCP I/O completes, a lost response becomes
        <code>Unknown</code>, duplicate dispatch is suppressed, and
        authoritative reconciliation commits idempotently with one physical
        network call.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These are StateKnot profile tests, not substitutes for the official MCP
      requirement set. Read the <a href="/docs/mcp-remote-tool/"
        >strict Remote Tool contract</a
      > or the <a
        href="https://github.com/StateKnot/StateKnot/blob/main/docs/mcp-conformance.md"
        >complete evidence report</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="mcp-conformance-gate-title">
    <h2 id="mcp-conformance-gate-title">Gate for a future claim</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Define and security-review a separate general MCP client surface.</li>
      <li>
        Implement every applicable scored client capability in one frozen
        requirement revision, including its authorization and request-state
        behavior.
      </li>
      <li>
        Run that exact official requirement set in mandatory CI without a
        misleading expected-failure blanket.
      </li>
      <li>
        Publish the runner identity, generated checks, platform, date, and
        result as a release artifact.
      </li>
      <li>
        Keep strict profile tests and PostgreSQL recovery proof as independent
        release gates.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
